{"timeLimit":2400,"questions":[{"question":"______ is the difference between the highest and the lowest values in a given data.","options":["mode","mean","median","range","rank"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["Range \\(=\\) highest \\(-\\) lowest."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Statistics","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"A student correctly added the two two-digit numbers on the left of the board and got the answer \\(137\\). What answer will he get if he adds the two four-digit numbers on the right of the board?","options":["\\(13737\\)","\\(14747\\)","\\(137137\\)","\\(13837\\)","\\(23737\\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(ADCB + CBAD = 1010(A + C) + 101(B + D) = 101 \\times [10(A + C) + (B + D)]\\).","\\(10(A + C) + (B + D) = AB + CD = 137\\), so the answer is \\(101 \\times 137 = 13837\\)."],"hint":"","image":"/exam-archive/competitions/scholastic/junior-secondary/4th-edition/first-Round/q2.svg","topic":"Number","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"The sum of three consecutive odd numbers is \\(87\\). The median of the three numbers is:","options":["\\(13\\)","\\(17\\)","\\(29\\)","\\(31\\)","\\(33\\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["The middle number is \\(87 \\div 3 = 29\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Statistics","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"If the bearing of \\(Y\\) from \\(X\\) is \\(282^{\\circ}\\), what is the bearing of \\(X\\) from \\(Y\\)?","options":["\\(270^{\\circ}\\)","\\(148^{\\circ}\\)","\\(112^{\\circ}\\)","\\(102^{\\circ}\\)","\\(78^{\\circ}\\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["The back bearing is \\(282 - 180 = 102^{\\circ}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Bearings","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"The length of a football pitch can be divided into \\(8\\) parts, each \\(12.5\\text{ cm}\\) long. How many parts, each \\(20\\text{ cm}\\) long, can be obtained from the pitch?","options":["\\(20\\)","\\(15\\)","\\(13\\)","\\(10\\)","\\(5\\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["Length \\(= 8 \\times 12.5 = 100\\text{ cm}\\); \\(100 \\div 20 = 5\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Measurement","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"If \\(\\frac{a}{2} = 2b - c\\), find the value of \\(b\\) when \\(a = 11\\) and \\(c = 23\\).","options":["\\(17\\)","\\(7\\)","\\(28.5\\)","\\(14.25\\)","\\(16\\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(5.5 = 2b - 23\\), so \\(2b = 28.5\\) and \\(b = 14.25\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Algebra","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Find the smallest number that \\(48\\) must be multiplied by to give a perfect square.","options":["\\(15\\)","\\(10\\)","\\(6\\)","\\(5\\)","\\(3\\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(48 = 2^{4} \\times 3\\); multiply by \\(3\\) to get \\(144 = 12^{2}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Indices","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Find the radius of a circle whose circumference is \\(44\\text{ cm}\\).","options":["\\(44\\text{ cm}\\)","\\(28\\text{ cm}\\)","\\(22\\text{ cm}\\)","\\(14\\text{ cm}\\)","\\(7\\text{ cm}\\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times r = 44\\), so \\(r = 7\\text{ cm}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Circles","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Express \\(0.0104\\) in standard form.","options":["\\(10.4 \\times 10^{-1}\\)","\\(1.04 \\times 10^{-2}\\)","\\(1.04 \\times 10^{-3}\\)","\\(0.0104 \\times 10^{-4}\\)","\\(1.4 \\times 10^{-2}\\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["Move the point two places right: \\(1.04 \\times 10^{-2}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Standard Form","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Find the H.C.F. of \\(24a^{2}\\) and \\(36ab\\).","options":["\\(4a\\)","\\(4a^{2}b\\)","\\(6a^{2}b\\)","\\(12ab^{2}\\)","\\(12a\\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["HCF of \\(24\\) and \\(36\\) is \\(12\\); the common letter is \\(a\\). HCF \\(= 12a\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"HCF and LCM","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Decrease \\(5\\text{ kg}\\) by \\(15\\%\\).","options":["\\(3.75\\text{ kg}\\)","\\(4.75\\text{ kg}\\)","\\(4.25\\text{ kg}\\)","\\(6.25\\text{ kg}\\)","\\(7.50\\text{ kg}\\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(85\\%\\) of \\(5 = 4.25\\text{ kg}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Percentages","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"The total of the angles in a heptagon is","options":["\\(900^{\\circ}\\)","\\(1080^{\\circ}\\)","\\(990^{\\circ}\\)","\\(720^{\\circ}\\)","\\(360^{\\circ}\\)"],"correctIndex":0,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\((7 - 2) \\times 180^{\\circ} = 900^{\\circ}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Polygons","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Given \\(9, 7, 11, 13, 2, 4, 5\\) and \\(5\\), find the mean of the data.","options":["\\(7\\)","\\(9\\)","\\(11\\)","\\(13\\)","\\(5\\)"],"correctIndex":0,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["Sum \\(= 56\\); \\(56 \\div 8 = 7\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Statistics","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"The reciprocal of \\(0.052\\) to two significant figures is?","options":["\\(5.2\\)","\\(9.2\\)","\\(1.09\\)","\\(19\\)","\\(20\\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(1 \\div 0.052 = 19.23\\ldots \\approx 19\\) to two significant figures."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Approximation","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"An ant walks along the sides of an equilateral triangle (see diagram). Its velocity is \\(5\\text{ cm/min}\\) along the first side, \\(15\\text{ cm/min}\\) along the second and \\(20\\text{ cm/min}\\) along the third. With which average velocity in cm/min does the ant walk once around the entire triangle?","options":["\\(10\\)","\\(\\frac{180}{19}\\)","\\(\\frac{40}{3}\\)","\\(\\frac{80}{11}\\)","\\(15\\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["For side \\(L\\): time \\(= \\frac{L}{5} + \\frac{L}{15} + \\frac{L}{20} = \\frac{19L}{60}\\).","Average speed \\(= \\frac{3L}{19L/60} = \\frac{180}{19}\\)."],"hint":"","image":"/exam-archive/competitions/scholastic/junior-secondary/4th-edition/first-Round/q15.svg","topic":"Speed","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Find the sum of the prime factors of \\(100\\).","options":["\\(5\\)","\\(7\\)","\\(8\\)","\\(10\\)","\\(12\\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(100 = 2^{2} \\times 5^{2}\\); \\(2 + 5 = 7\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Prime Factors","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"On every sale of goods worth \\(₦1.5\\) million, there is a commission of \\(₦5550.00\\). If an agent delivers \\(₦0.75\\) million, find his commission.","options":["\\(₦1250.00\\)","\\(₦2250.00\\)","\\(₦2775.00\\)","\\(₦4150.00\\)","\\(₦7150.00\\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(0.75\\) million is half of \\(1.5\\) million: \\(5550 \\div 2 = ₦2775\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Proportion","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"A coin is tossed three times. What is the probability of getting at least one head?","options":["\\(0\\)","\\(0.527\\)","\\(0.625\\)","\\(0.875\\)","\\(1\\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(1 - P(\\text{no head}) = 1 - \\frac{1}{8} = 0.875\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Probability","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"The cube root of \\(4\\tfrac{17}{27}\\) is:","options":["\\(1\\tfrac{2}{3}\\)","\\(6\\tfrac{1}{8}\\)","\\(3\\tfrac{1}{2}\\)","\\(6\\tfrac{1}{4}\\)","\\(3\\tfrac{3}{4}\\)"],"correctIndex":0,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(4\\tfrac{17}{27} = \\frac{125}{27}\\); \\(\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{125}{27}} = \\frac{5}{3} = 1\\tfrac{2}{3}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Indices","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"The height of a tree is equal to the length of its shadow. The angle of elevation of the sun is:","options":["\\(0^{\\circ}\\)","\\(30^{\\circ}\\)","\\(45^{\\circ}\\)","\\(60^{\\circ}\\)","\\(90^{\\circ}\\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(\\tan\\theta = 1\\), so \\(\\theta = 45^{\\circ}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Trigonometry","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Which of the numbers \\(a, b, c, d\\) and \\(e\\) is smallest if \\(a - 4 = b + 1 = c - 2 = d + 6 = e - 7\\)?","options":["\\(a\\)","\\(b\\)","\\(c\\)","\\(d\\)","\\(e\\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["Call the common value \\(k\\): \\(a = k + 4\\), \\(b = k - 1\\), \\(c = k + 2\\), \\(d = k - 6\\), \\(e = k + 7\\).","\\(d\\) is the smallest."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Algebra","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"The area of the large square is \\(16\\text{ cm}^{2}\\) and the area of each small square is \\(1\\text{ cm}^{2}\\). What is the total area of the central flower in \\(\\text{cm}^{2}\\)?","options":["\\(3\\)","\\(\\frac{7}{2}\\)","\\(4\\)","\\(\\frac{11}{2}\\)","\\(6\\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["The large square is \\(4 \\times 4\\). Each white triangle has a \\(2\\text{ cm}\\) base on a side and its tip at the centre: area \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times 2 \\times 2 = 2\\).","Flower \\(= 16 - 4 \\times 1 - 4 \\times 2 = 4\\text{ cm}^{2}\\)."],"hint":"","image":"/exam-archive/competitions/scholastic/junior-secondary/4th-edition/first-Round/q22.svg","topic":"Area","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"\\(110_{\\text{two}} \\times 101_{\\text{two}} =\\)","options":["\\(30_{\\text{ten}}\\)","\\(34_{\\text{ten}}\\)","\\(64_{\\text{ten}}\\)","\\(121_{\\text{ten}}\\)","\\(1111_{\\text{ten}}\\)"],"correctIndex":0,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(6 \\times 5 = 30\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Number Bases","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Eight people meet for a particular programme. Each person shakes hands once with every other person present. How many handshakes took place?","options":["\\(16\\)","\\(28\\)","\\(49\\)","\\(56\\)","\\(64\\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(\\frac{8 \\times 7}{2} = 28\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Counting","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"What is the result when \\(1515\\) is divided by \\(15\\)?","options":["\\(11\\)","\\(101\\)","\\(1001\\)","\\(10001\\)","Not an integer"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(1515 = 15 \\times 101\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Number","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Which of the following values is largest?","options":["\\(2 + 3 + 0 + 7\\)","\\(2 \\times 3 + 0 + 7\\)","\\(2 + 3 \\times 0 + 7\\)","\\(2 + 3 + 0 \\times 7\\)","\\(2 \\times 3 \\times 0 \\times 7\\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["The values are \\(12, 13, 9, 5, 0\\); the largest is \\(13\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Order of Operations","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"John has \\(4\\) sisters and \\(7\\) brothers. His sister Jane has \\(P\\) sisters and \\(Q\\) brothers. What is the sum of \\(P\\) and \\(Q\\)?","options":["\\(3\\)","\\(5\\)","\\(9\\)","\\(10\\)","\\(11\\)"],"correctIndex":4,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["Jane has \\(3\\) sisters, and \\(8\\) brothers (John's \\(7\\) plus John).","\\(3 + 8 = 11\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Logic","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Each interior angle of a regular polygon is \\(2y + 36\\). If each exterior angle of the polygon is \\(2y\\), find the value of \\(y\\).","options":["\\(34^{\\circ}\\)","\\(36^{\\circ}\\)","\\(72^{\\circ}\\)","\\(87^{\\circ}\\)","\\(90^{\\circ}\\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["Interior \\(+\\) exterior \\(= 180^{\\circ}\\): \\(4y + 36 = 180\\), so \\(y = 36\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Polygons","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"A sector of a circle of radius \\(8\\text{ cm}\\) has an angle of \\(135^{\\circ}\\). What is its area in \\(\\text{cm}^{2}\\) in terms of \\(\\pi\\)?","options":["\\(9\\pi\\)","\\(24\\pi\\)","\\(64\\pi\\)","\\(84\\pi\\)","\\(144\\pi\\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(\\frac{135}{360} \\times \\pi \\times 8^{2} = 24\\pi\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Circles","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"If \\(A = \\frac{1}{2}(a + b)h\\), express \\(h\\) in terms of \\(A\\), \\(a\\) and \\(b\\).","options":["\\(A - \\frac{1}{2}(a + b)\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{2}(a + b)A\\)","\\(\\frac{2A}{a + b}\\)","\\(\\frac{A}{2(a + b)}\\)","\\(\\frac{a + b}{2A}\\)"],"correctIndex":2,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(2A = (a + b)h\\), so \\(h = \\frac{2A}{a + b}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Change of Subject","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"If \\(\\cos B = \\frac{5}{13}\\), find \\(\\frac{\\tan B}{\\cos B}\\).","options":["\\(\\frac{3}{13}\\)","\\(\\frac{156}{25}\\)","\\(\\frac{12}{13}\\)","\\(\\frac{5}{18}\\)","\\(\\frac{11}{18}\\)"],"correctIndex":1,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["\\(\\sin B = \\frac{12}{13}\\), \\(\\tan B = \\frac{12}{5}\\).","\\(\\frac{\\tan B}{\\cos B} = \\frac{12}{5} \\times \\frac{13}{5} = \\frac{156}{25}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Trigonometry","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"Approximate \\(5.7255\\) to the nearest thousandth.","options":["\\(5.7\\)","\\(5.725\\)","\\(5.7255\\)","\\(5.726\\)","\\(5.73\\)"],"correctIndex":3,"answer":null,"accept":null,"explanation":["The ten-thousandths digit is \\(5\\), so round up: \\(5.726\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Approximation","type":"objective","section":null},{"question":"The ages of a brother and his younger sister sum to \\(44\\). In five years, the brother will be twice as old as his sister. Find the age of the sister.","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(13\\)","accept":["13"],"explanation":["\\(b + s = 44\\) and \\(b + 5 = 2(s + 5)\\), so \\(b = 2s + 5\\).","\\(3s + 5 = 44\\), so \\(s = 13\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Algebra","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"Find the value of \\(x\\) for which \\(312_{\\text{four}} + 52_{x} = 96_{\\text{ten}}\\).","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(x = 8\\)","accept":["x = 8"],"explanation":["\\(312_{\\text{four}} = 48 + 4 + 2 = 54\\).","\\(52_{x} = 96 - 54 = 42\\), so \\(5x + 2 = 42\\) and \\(x = 8\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Number Bases","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"Twenty girls and \\(y\\) boys sat for an examination. The mean marks obtained by the girls and boys were \\(52\\) and \\(57\\) respectively. If the total score for both girls and boys was \\(2750\\), find \\(y\\).","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(y = 30\\)","accept":["y = 30"],"explanation":["Girls' total \\(= 20 \\times 52 = 1040\\).","\\(57y = 2750 - 1040 = 1710\\), so \\(y = 30\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Statistics","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"Harold made a plum pie to take on a picnic. He was able to eat only \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) of the pie, and he left the rest for his friends. A moose came by and ate \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) of what Harold left behind. After that, a porcupine ate \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) of what the moose left behind. How much of the original pie still remained after the porcupine left?","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)","accept":["1/3"],"explanation":["Harold left \\(\\frac{3}{4}\\); the moose left \\(\\frac{2}{3} \\times \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{1}{2}\\).","The porcupine left \\(\\frac{2}{3} \\times \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{1}{3}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Fractions","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"In the diagram \\(QSR\\) is a straight line, \\(\\angle QPS = 12^{\\circ}\\) and \\(PQ = PS = RS\\). How big is \\(\\angle QPR\\)?","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(54^{\\circ}\\)","accept":["54°"],"explanation":["\\(PQ = PS\\): \\(\\angle PSQ = \\frac{180 - 12}{2} = 84^{\\circ}\\), so \\(\\angle PSR = 96^{\\circ}\\).","\\(PS = RS\\): \\(\\angle SPR = \\frac{180 - 96}{2} = 42^{\\circ}\\).","\\(\\angle QPR = 12 + 42 = 54^{\\circ}\\)."],"hint":"","image":"/exam-archive/competitions/scholastic/junior-secondary/4th-edition/first-Round/q37.svg","topic":"Triangles","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"A sector of a circle of radius \\(7\\text{ cm}\\) subtending an angle of \\(216^{\\circ}\\) at the centre of the circle is bent to form a cone. What is the base radius of the cone?","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(4.2\\text{ cm}\\)","accept":["4.2 cm"],"explanation":["The arc becomes the base circumference: \\(\\frac{216}{360} \\times 2\\pi \\times 7 = 2\\pi r\\).","\\(r = 0.6 \\times 7 = 4.2\\text{ cm}\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Mensuration","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"Factorise completely \\(16x^{2} - 25\\).","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\((4x - 5)(4x + 5)\\)","accept":["(4x - 5)(4x + 5)"],"explanation":["Difference of two squares: \\((4x)^{2} - 5^{2} = (4x - 5)(4x + 5)\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Factorisation","type":"subjective","section":null},{"question":"There are four more girls than boys in Ms. Ann's class of \\(28\\) students. What is the ratio of the number of girls to the number of boys in her class?","options":[],"correctIndex":null,"answer":"\\(4 : 3\\)","accept":["4 : 3"],"explanation":["\\(b + (b + 4) = 28\\), so \\(b = 12\\) and \\(g = 16\\).","\\(16 : 12 = 4 : 3\\)."],"hint":"","image":null,"topic":"Ratio","type":"subjective","section":null}]}